    "https://careers.umich.edu/job_detail/284090": {
      "title": "CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR",
      "description": "CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR | U-M Careers Skip to main content twitter rss addthis Utility Login Help and FAQ CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR Main navigation Home Search Jobs Benefits Choose Michigan Temporary Employment Student Employment Career Development Help and FAQ Apply Now How to Apply Candidates should contact: Karl Desch, MD Clinical Professor of Pediatrics, Search Committee Chair Division of Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine E-mail: [email protected] . Job Summary University of Michigan C.S. Mott Children's Hospital Division of Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine The Division of Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine within the Department of Pediatrics at C.S. Mott Children's Hospital, University of Michigan, is expanding in Southeast Michigan and invites applications for academic faculty positions in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine. We seek candidates with a demonstrated commitment to providing exceptional care for patients and families in our Level IV NICU, as well as a strong interest in advancing their academic careers. Successful candidates will be able to convey their passion for the field and their potential to contribute meaningfully to our tripartite mission of research, medical education, and clinical care. C.S. Mott Children's Hospital is ranked first in the state by USNWR , third in the region, and is nationally ranked in all ten specialties, including Neonatology. The Brandon Newborn Intensive Care Unit, a 58-bed single patient room Level 4 NICU within the freestanding C.S. Mott Children's Hospital and Von Voigtlander Women's Hospital, is an integral part of Michigan Medicine's main medical campus in Ann Arbor (4900 deliveries, 900 admissions annually, 70% inborn). Neonatologists, collaborate closely with the Congenital Heart Center, remotely supervise APPs or fellows on medical transports in a large geographic catchment area, attend high risk deliveries, participate in prenatal consultation and care coordination in collaboration with maternal-fetal medicine, palliative care, and pediatric and surgical subspecialists in the Fetal Diagnostic Center, which offers advanced fetal procedures and fetal surgery. Our Division and Department offer opportunities to participate in clinical, translational, bioethics, health services, global health, bench and educational research. Your clinical responsibilities will be under the direction of the Division's Service Chief, Dr. Parul Cham, and the Division Director, Dr. Naomi Laventhal. These responsibilities will include serving as an attending physician in the Brandon Newborn Intensive Care Unit. In this role, you will serve as the rounding attending on one of our clinical service teams for approximately ten to fourteen weeks per 12-month year, with coverage consisting of seven day shifts per week during assigned service weeks. You will also serve as the resource attending or consult attending, depending on your expertise and interests, for approximately five to ten weeks per year, with coverage consisting of five day shifts per week. In addition, you will participate in night call, including both weekday and weekend nights, which will be divided among Division faculty based on appointed effort. Night call is currently in-house and includes either supplemental payment for each night of call or equivalent remuneration over the course of the year. The specific distribution of NICU attending service and night call will be determined at the discretion of the Service Chief and Division Director. These estimates may be affected by unexpected changes in Division staffing. While on service and on call, you will also be expected to participate in the clinical training of medical students, nurse practitioner students, house officers, and neonatology fellows, as well as in the supervision and education of neonatal nurse practitioners and/or physician assistants. Work site locations may change based on staffing needs. Required Qualifications* Applicants must hold an MD or DO degree and be board-certified or board-eligible in Neonatal-Perinatal Medicine by the position start date. Modes of Work Positions that are eligible for hybrid or mobile/remote work mode are at the discretion of the hiring department. Work agreements are reviewed annually at a minimum and are subject to change at any time, and for any reason, throughout the course of employment. Learn more about the work modes . Underfill Statement Note: This position is posted as Clinical Instructor/Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor. Rank of selected candidate is dependent upon qualifications. Background Screening University of Michigan Health System conducts background screening and pre-employment drug testing on job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent job offer and may use a third party administrator to conduct background screenings. Background screenings are performed in compliance with the Fair Credit Report Act. Application Deadline Job openings are posted for a minimum of seven calendar days.  The review and selection process may begin as early as the eighth day after posting. This opening may be removed from posting boards and filled anytime after the minimum posting period has ended . U-M EEO Statement The University of Michigan is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Job Detail Job Opening ID 284090 Working Title CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR Job Title CLINICAL PROFESSOR Work Location Ann Arbor Campus Ann Arbor, MI Modes of Work Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular FLSA Status Exempt Organizational Group Medical School Department MM Pediatrics-Neonatal Perinat Posting Begin/End Date 10/08/2026 - 1/06/2027 Career Interest Instructional - Regular Clinical Apply Now Contact Footer Non-discrimination Statement Accessibility Security and Safety Annual Report Labor Law Notices Department of Labor Notices of Filing © 2026 The Regents of the University of Michigan"
    },
    "https://careers.umich.edu/job_detail/283730": {
      "title": "CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR",
      "description": "CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR | U-M Careers Skip to main content twitter rss addthis Utility Login Help and FAQ CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR Main navigation Home Search Jobs Benefits Choose Michigan Temporary Employment Student Employment Career Development Help and FAQ Apply Now How to Apply Interested candidates should E-mail curriculum vitae and a cover letter to: Rajen Mody, MD, MS Ruth Heyn Professor of Pediatric Oncology Director, Division of Pediatric Hematology/Oncology/ BMT Director, Pediatric Phase-I and Experimental Therapeutics Program Michigan Medicine D4206 Medical Professional Building, SPC 5718 [email protected] Job Summary A faculty position is available for a Pediatric Hematologist Oncologist with strong interest and skills in patient care, teaching, and research.  This position will involve collaboration between the Pediatric Hematology/Oncology and Bone Marrow Transplant (PHO-BMT) program at Michigan Medicine and the Pediatric Hematology/Oncology program at Trinity Health Oakland (THO) or another off-site affiliate. The rank will be dependent on experience. Responsibilities will be primarily clinical, with approximately 50% effort at THO or another off-site affiliate and 50% at Michigan Medicine. These percentages may change as patient volume changes at THO and other off-site locations. Responsibilities at Michigan Medicine will include providing care on both the outpatient and inpatient PHO-BMT services.  This position will include sharing services with other Pediatric Hematologist Oncologists, teaching medical students and residents, clinical supervision of nurses and other allied health providers, and involvement in clinical trials in oncology. Required Qualifications* Candidates must possess an M.D. or D.O. degree, must have completed a fellowship in Pediatric Hematology/Oncology, be board certified in Pediatrics and board certified/eligible Pediatric Hematology/Oncology, and be eligible for licensure in the State of Michigan. Proven excellence in clinical care and teaching is required. Why Join Michigan Medicine? Michigan Medicine is one of the largest health care complexes in the world and has been the site of many groundbreaking medical and technological advancements since the opening of the U-M Medical School in 1850. Michigan Medicine is comprised of over 30,000 employees and our vision is to attract, inspire, and develop outstanding people in medicine, sciences, and healthcare to become one of the world's most distinguished academic health systems.  In some way, great or small, every person here helps to advance this world-class institution. Work at Michigan Medicine and become a victor for the greater good. What Benefits can you Look Forward to? Excellent medical, dental and vision coverage effective on your very first day 2:1 Match on retirement savings Modes of Work Positions that are eligible for hybrid or mobile/remote work mode are at the discretion of the hiring department. Work agreements are reviewed annually at a minimum and are subject to change at any time, and for any reason, throughout the course of employment. Learn more about the work modes . Underfill Statement This position is posted as Clinical Instructor/Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor/Clinical Professor. The rank of the selected candidate will depend upon candidate's qualifications. U-M EEO Statement The University of Michigan is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Job Detail Job Opening ID 283730 Working Title CLINICAL INSTRUCTOR-CLINICAL PROFESSOR Job Title CLINICAL PROFESSOR Work Location Ann Arbor Campus Ann Arbor, MI Modes of Work Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular FLSA Status Exempt Organizational Group Medical School Department MM Pediatrics-Hematology Oncol Posting Begin/End Date 9/30/2026 - 10/30/2026 Career Interest Instructional - Regular Clinical Apply Now Contact Footer Non-discrimination Statement Accessibility Security and Safety Annual Report Labor Law Notices Department of Labor Notices of Filing © 2026 The Regents of the University of Michigan"
