    "https://careers.umich.edu/job_detail/282681": {
      "title": "Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Restorative Dentistry Department of Cariology, Restorative Sciences, and Endodontics (CRSE)",
      "description": "Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Restorative Dentistry Department of Cariology, Restorative Sciences, and Endodontics (CRSE) | U-M Careers Skip to main content twitter rss addthis Utility Login Help and FAQ Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Restorative Dentistry Department of Cariology, Restorative Sciences, and Endodontics (CRSE) Main navigation Home Search Jobs Benefits Choose Michigan Temporary Employment Student Employment Career Development Help and FAQ Apply Now How to Apply \"ATTENTION FACULTY APPLICANTS: DO NOT USE THE \"APPLY NOW\" BUTTON AT THE TOP OF THIS PAGE. If you are interested in applying for this position within the School of Dentistry, PLEASE APPLY HERE \" Applicants should submit the following application materials via the secure website : Curriculum vitae Statement of interest Names of three professional references Questions regarding the position and responsibilities should be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Carlos Gonzalez ( [email protected] ). For questions regarding the application or search process, please contact administrative support staff, Melanie LaPointe ( [email protected] ). Applications will be accepted and evaluated on an ongoing basis until the positions are filled. To optimize your chances, please apply as soon as possible. The search committee plans to begin reviewing applications in early October 2026. Employment is contingent on the successful completion of a background check. Candidates may be required to submit a self-disclosure form as well as an authorization to release information form. Job Summary The University of Michigan School of Dentistry invites applications for three full-time clinical track faculty positions at the Clinical Assistant or Associate Professor level in the Department of Cariology, Restorative Sciences and Endodontics (CRSE), Division of Restorative Dentistry. The salary and rank will be commensurate with experience and credentials. The School and the CRSE Department are fully engaged in supporting state of the art dental education that includes evidence-based dentistry, multi-disciplinary education, and digital dentistry. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to, providing didactic, pre-clinical and clinical education, and summative/formative student assessment at the pre-doctoral and/or graduate restorative/cariology level. The successful candidate for this position must have a Doctor of Dental Surgery/Dental Medicine (DDS/DMD) degree or equivalent and the ability to be licensed in Michigan. Candidates should demonstrate a strong background in advanced operative/restorative dentistry, cariology, biomaterials, digital dentistry, and tooth replacement therapy including implant-supported restorations. Preference will be given to candidates holding an Advanced Clinical Education Program Certificate and/or MS in Operative or Restorative Dentistry, as well as some teaching, mentorship and research experience. The CRSE Department has an active mentorship program and will provide ample opportunity for development of collaborative research projects. This position offers opportunities for scholarly activities, continuing education, and service, including the ability to establish a robust intramural clinical practice with the UM SOD Dental Faculty Associates Clinic (DFA). Further information about the CRSE Department may be found on the department website . Required Qualifications* The successful candidate for this position must have a Doctor of Dental Surgery/Dental Medicine (DDS/DMD) degree or equivalent and the ability to be licensed in Michigan. Candidates should demonstrate a strong background in advanced operative/restorative dentistry, cariology, biomaterials, digital dentistry, and tooth replacement therapy including implant-supported restorations. Preference will be given to candidates holding an Advanced Clinical Education Program Certificate and/or MS in Operative or Restorative Dentistry, as well as some teaching, mentorship and research experience. Modes of Work Positions that are eligible for hybrid or mobile/remote work mode are at the discretion of the hiring department. Work agreements are reviewed annually at a minimum and are subject to change at any time, and for any reason, throughout the course of employment. Learn more about the work modes . Underfill Statement This position is posted as Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor. The rank of the selected candidate will depend upon candidate's qualifications. Background Screening The University of Michigan conducts background checks on all job candidates upon acceptance of a contingent offer and may use a third party administrator to conduct background checks.  Background checks are performed in compliance with the Fair Credit Reporting Act. U-M EEO Statement The University of Michigan is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Job Detail Job Opening ID 282681 Working Title Clinical Track Assistant/Associate Professor of Restorative Dentistry Department of Cariology, Restorative Sciences, and Endodontics (CRSE) Job Title CLINICAL ASSOC PROF Work Location Ann Arbor Campus Ann Arbor, MI Modes of Work Onsite Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular FLSA Status Exempt Organizational Group School Dentistry Department DENTCariology,Restor Sci &Endo Posting Begin/End Date 9/03/2026 - 11/02/2026 Career Interest Instructional - Regular Clinical Apply Now Contact Footer Non-discrimination Statement Accessibility Security and Safety Annual Report Labor Law Notices Department of Labor Notices of Filing © 2026 The Regents of the University of Michigan"
    },
    "https://careers.umich.edu/job_detail/282155": {
      "title": "CLINICAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR",
      "description": "CLINICAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR | U-M Careers Skip to main content twitter rss addthis Utility Login Help and FAQ CLINICAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR Main navigation Home Search Jobs Benefits Choose Michigan Temporary Employment Student Employment Career Development Help and FAQ Apply Now How to Apply The confidential review of applications will occur September 2026 through December 2026 until the position is filled. A cover letter and current curriculum vitae must be uploaded online via the U-M Careers website http://careers.umich.edu/ for this Job ID 282155. In addition to applying online, applicants are requested to send the following to the Office of Human Resources at [email protected] : Teaching statement which should describe teaching philosophy, experience in teaching across programs and settings (i.e., didactic and clinical) Practice statement Scholarship (research) statement that includes a statement of impact of his/her/their work in the first paragraph Service statement If selected to move forward in the process, applicants will be asked to submit additional materials as noted in the School of Nursing Faculty Handbook including professional letters of recommendation, transcripts of your highest degrees, and compliance requirements. For further information regarding these positions please contact [email protected] . For further information regarding these positions, please contact Patricia Hershberger, PhD, APRN, FNP-BC, FAAN at: [email protected] . Job Summary The University of Michigan School of Nursing (UMSN) is a vibrant community of scholars, educators, clinicians, and innovators embedded within one of the world's leading public research universities. Consistently ranked among the nation's top nursing schools, we are committed to advancing health and health equity through research, education leadership, and service. Our faculty generate knowledge that improves lives, informs policy, strengthens healthcare delivery, and addresses pressing local and global health challenges. The UMSN invites applications for a full-time, 12-month clinical track faculty position ideally beginning in January 2027. We seek accomplished board-certified Pediatric Nurse Practitioners, clinical educators, and clinical scholars who demonstrate excellence in advanced practice nursing, teaching, mentorship, scholarship, and service. We welcome both emerging and established clinical leaders whose expertise contributes to the preparation of future advanced practice nurses and the advancement of evidence-based healthcare. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to innovative teaching, interprofessional collaboration, and clinical excellence. Applicants should have experience teaching in undergraduate and/or graduate nursing programs and be actively engaged in clinical practice. preference will be given to Pediatric Nurse Practitioners with expertise in traditional pediatric primary care. Candidates must demonstrate commitment to student mentorship, innovative clinical education, and the integration of teaching, practice, scholarship and service. Interest in global health practice is desirable. Courses are delivered both online and in person, and this is an on-site position. The search will be conducted during the Fall term of the 2026-2027 academic year, with application reviews beginning in September 2026. Applicants will be considered for the ranks listed above depending on applicant experience and scholarship productivity. Required Qualifications* NECESSARY QUALIFICATIONS Doctorate in Nursing. A nursing license in the State of Michigan is required for this position (current licensure or willingness to obtain licensure). A specialty certification in the State of Michigan is required for this position. You must hold a Pediatric Nurse Practitioner Board Certification (CPNP-PC) from the Pediatric Nursing Certification Board (PNCB). Demonstrated excellent communication, networking and relationship building skills. Current clinical experience in a practice relevant role. Demonstrated ability to participate in the development and implementation of innovative curricular activities. Ability to collaborate with faculty and clinical partners to develop and sustain high-quality educational programs. Evidence of increasing service to the profession and academic community. Evidence of clinically relevant scholarship that advances advanced practice nursing and healthcare outcomes. Scholarship may include peer-reviewed publications, evidence-based practice initiatives, quality improvement projects, program evaluation, guideline development, dissemination activities, and grant-related work. Prior to the start date must be in compliance with all health requirements including standard precautions such as Basic Life Support (BLS) certification, orientations, licenses/certifications, policies, and procedures both internal and external to the University for your assigned classroom(s) and/or clinical site(s). Ability to promote the School of Nursing's Declaration of Values to E mpower each other to interrupt or disrupt disrespect; P ractice communication that is beneficial, kind and true; I nspire and be inspired by our members' worth, significance and integrity; C ultivate respect for ourselves and others routinely, publicly and privately. Additional Qualifications for the Clinical Associate Professor Rank - Demonstrated excellence and sustained impact in clinical and/or didactic teaching. Evidence of leadership in advanced practice education, curriculum development, clinical program innovation, or professional organizations. Sustained record of clinically relevant scholarship with regional or national recognition. Significant service contributions to the profession, academic community, healthcare organizations, or clinical initiatives. Modes of Work Positions that are eligible for hybrid or mobile/remote work mode are at the discretion of the hiring department. Work agreements are reviewed annually at a minimum and are subject to change at any time, and for any reason, throughout the course of employment. Learn more about the work modes . Underfill Statement This position is posted as Clinical Assistant Professor/Clinical Associate Professor. The rank of the selected candidate will depend upon the selected candidate's qualifications. Application Deadline Complete application packets must be submitted by October 31, 2026. The Faculty Search Committee will review applications beginning in the Fall 2026. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply. U-M EEO Statement The University of Michigan is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Job Detail Job Opening ID 282155 Working Title CLINICAL ASSISTANT PROFESSOR/CLINICAL ASSOCIATE PROFESSOR Job Title CLINICAL ASSOC PROF Work Location Ann Arbor Campus Ann Arbor, MI Modes of Work Onsite Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular FLSA Status Exempt Organizational Group School Nursing Department School of Nursing Posting Begin/End Date 8/23/2026 - 10/31/2026 Career Interest Instructional - Regular Clinical Apply Now Contact Footer Non-discrimination Statement Accessibility Security and Safety Annual Report Labor Law Notices Department of Labor Notices of Filing © 2026 The Regents of the University of Michigan"
    },
